		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=963#p963"><![CDATA[
If you can get that and restitution and the ability to make objects ride IPO objects ready by 2.43 that would be great. And then we can say good by and good riddance to Sumo and other game engines plugging into it once the plugin system is done can use it <img class="smilies" src="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/images/smilies/icon_biggrin.gif" width="15" height="15" alt=":D" title="Very Happy"> <br><br>I've been looking for years to find the ideal 3D engine and it looks like the Blender engine will be suitable for decent games with good physics by 2.43.<br><br><br>BTW: say you have an object animated with an armature, would it be possible for the different collider objects to be animated with the armature object to allow for more precise collision detection?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=421">Icoxo</a> — Mon May 01, 2006 9:22 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
